@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix :     <http://example.org/odp#>.

:Ontology a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Sprinkler Use Case" ;
    rdfs:comment "An ontology for the sprinkler use case.".

:Event a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Event" ;
    rdfs:comment "Abstract class for events.".

:RainySeason a :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Rainy Season" ;
    rdfs:comment "Event representing the rainy season.".

:SprinklerOn a :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Sprinkler On" ;
    rdfs:comment "Event representing the sprinkler being on.".

:Raining a :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Raining" ;
    rdfs:comment "Event representing it is raining.".

:PavementWet a :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Pavement Wet" ;
    rdfs:comment "Event representing the pavement is wet.".

:PavementSlippery a :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Pavement Slippery" ;
    rdfs:comment "Event representing the pavement is slippery.".

:CausalRelation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Causal Relation" ;
    rdfs:comment "Property for causal relations between events.".

:EffectWeight a xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "Effect Weight" ;
    rdfs:comment "Datatype for effect weights.".

:Causes rdfs:subPropertyOf :CausalRelation ;
    rdfs:label "Causes" ;
    rdfs:comment "Subproperty for direct causal relations.".

:Mediates rdfs:subPropertyOf :CausalRelation ;
    rdfs:label "Mediates" ;
    rdfs:comment "Subproperty for causal relations mediated by another event.".

:CausallyRelatedTo domain :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Causally Related To" ;
    rdfs:comment "Domain for causal relations.".

:HasEffectWeight domain :CausalRelation ;
    range :EffectWeight ;
    rdfs:label "Has Effect Weight" ;
    rdfs:comment "Property for the effect weight of a causal relation.".

:IsMediatedBy domain :CausalRelation ;
    range :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Is Mediated By" ;
    rdfs:comment "Property for the event that a causal relation is mediated by.".

:IsDirectlyCausedBy domain :Event ;
    range :Event ;
    rdfs:label "Is Directly Caused By" ;
    rdfs:comment "Property for the event that directly causes another event.".

Reasoning Summary:
1. Extracted atomic requirements:
   - The ontology represents events and causal relations between them.
   - There are five specific events: rainy season, sprinkler on, raining, pavement wet, and pavement slippery.
   - Causal relations have an effect weight.
   - Some causal relations are mediated by other events.